 # ImTube
 
-**ImTube** is a lightweight YouTube client for Linux, built for embedded systems
-(the **STM32MPU** / OpenSTLinux) and desktop PCs. It is a single-window,
-Dear ImGui application that searches, browses and plays YouTube videos with
-hardware-accelerated rendering and low CPU/RAM overhead.
+**ImTube** is a lightweight YouTube client. This fork targets old Macs first:
+G4/G5 PowerPC machines on Mac OS X 10.4/10.5, where a fixed-function OpenGL UI
+and a software-decoded 360p stream are all the hardware can carry. It still
+builds on Linux (desktop and the STM32MPU / OpenSTLinux board the project
+started on) and on x86 Macs. It is a single-window Dear ImGui application that
+searches, browses and plays YouTube videos with low CPU/RAM overhead.
 
 ![ImTube running (animated)](docs/screenshots/ImTube.gif)
 
 The whole stack is deliberately small: no Qt, no GTK, no Electron. The pieces are
-**Dear ImGui** (UI), **SDL3** (window/input), **GStreamer** (decode + playback),
-**yt-dlp** (YouTube extraction) and a thin render abstraction with **OpenGL ES 3.2**
-(default) and **Vulkan** (optional) backends.
+**Dear ImGui** (UI), **SDL2** (window/input; SDL3 and GLFW are alternatives),
+**GStreamer** (decode + playback), **yt-dlp** (YouTube extraction) and a thin
+render abstraction with a **legacy OpenGL** (fixed function, default) and an
+**OpenGL ES 3.2** backend.
 
