+Dependencies: CMake ≥ 3.16, a C++20 compiler, `pkg-config`, GStreamer 1.0 dev
+packages (`gstreamer-1.0`, `gstreamer-app-1.0`, `gstreamer-video-1.0`), SDL2
+(or SDL3 / GLFW 3), OpenGL headers (or `glesv2` + `egl` for the GLES backend),
+`libcurl` and nlohmann/json. Dear ImGui is either the vendored copy under
+`src/libraries/imgui` or a system package found through pkg-config (see below);
+stb is vendored under `src/libraries/stb`. SDL3 and nlohmann/json can be
+fetched by CMake when missing (`IMTUBE_ALLOW_FETCH`, on by default for native
+builds); package-based builds pass `-DIMTUBE_ALLOW_FETCH=OFF` to require
+system packages.
 
-### Linux PC (GLES, default)
+### Linux or macOS PC (SDL2 + legacy OpenGL, default)
 
 ```sh
-cmake --preset gles        # or: cmake -S . -B build -G Ninja
+cmake --preset sdl2-gl2    # or: cmake -S . -B build -G Ninja
 cmake --build build
 ./build/imtube
 ```
 
-### Linux PC (Vulkan)
+On macOS the build links the system `OpenGL.framework`, because that is the
+library behind the Cocoa video driver SDL2/SDL3/GLFW use there (also on
+10.4/10.5 PowerPC). It deliberately does not go through CMake's
+`find_package(OpenGL)`: with MacPorts' cmake (frameworks searched last) and
+the `mesa` port installed, that returns Mesa's X11 `libGL.dylib`, which never
+sees the Cocoa context. The symptom is a black window and
+`glGetString called without a rendering context` on stderr; ImTube now
+refuses to start in that state and says so. To run under XQuartz with Mesa
+instead, build with `-DIMTUBE_MACOS_GL=x11` and start with
+`SDL_VIDEODRIVER=x11`. The `[platform]` line on stderr shows the driver in
+use, e.g. `SDL 2.32.10 (cocoa)`.
+
+### PowerPC Macs (Mac OS X 10.4/10.5, MacPorts)
+
+Everything comes from ports: `sdl2` (or `glfw`), `imgui`, `gstreamer1` with
+the base/good/bad/libav plugin sets, `curl`, `nlohmann-json`, `ffmpeg`,
+`yt-dlp` with a JavaScript runtime (QuickJS), and a GCC with C++20.
+
+```sh
+cmake -S . -B build -G Ninja \
+    -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
+    -DIMTUBE_PLATFORM=sdl2 -DIMTUBE_RENDERER=gl2 \
+    -DIMTUBE_IMGUI=system -DIMTUBE_ALLOW_FETCH=OFF
+cmake --build build
+```
+
+The system Dear ImGui is expected in the layout of the MacPorts `imgui` port:
+a pkg-config module `imgui` (headers under `include/imgui`, static core
+library) plus the backend sources under `share/imgui/backends`. The port's
+`imgui.pc` may export `backendsdir=` to override that path.
